!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial 13: D&D 2024 Beacon Spell Slots
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| The D&D 2024 Beacon sheet keeps normal spell slots and Pact Magic slots
  --/| as two separate pools. This tutorial shows how ScriptCards reads and
  --/| writes those pools without mixing them together.
  --/|
  --/| HOW TO USE IT
  --/| 1. Select a D&D 2024 Beacon spellcaster with level-1 spell slots.
  --/| 2. Run this ScriptCard.
  --/| 3. A multiclass character with both normal and Pact slots is the best
  --/|    example because the output can show both pools at the same level.
  --/| 4. Any temporary slot changes are restored before the tutorial finishes.
  --/|
  --/| NORMAL SPELL SLOTS
  --/| Normal remaining slots are stored under:
  --/| sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel
  --/|
  --/| Level 1 uses FIRST, level 2 SECOND, level 3 THIRD, and so on through:
  --/| FOURTH, FIFTH, SIXTH, SEVENTH, EIGHTH, NINTH.
  --/|
  --/| ScriptCards also provides the familiar compatibility names:
  --/| lvl1_slots_total       = normal level-1 capacity
  --/| lvl1_slots_expended    = normal level-1 REMAINING slots
  --/|
  --/| IMPORTANT NAME WARNING
  --/| The historical name lvl1_slots_expended sounds like a count of used slots.
  --/| On the Beacon version of ScriptCards it means the number of normal slots
  --/| that are still available.
  --/|
  --/| In .135, reads and writes through lvlN_slots_expended deliberately use the
  --/| same remaining-slot value. ScriptCards routes writes directly to the
  --/| currentByLevel structured leaf instead of relying on Roll20's native setter,
  --/| whose numeric input was observed to use inverted/translated semantics.
  --/|
  --/| PACT MAGIC SLOTS
  --/| Pact remaining slots are stored separately under:
  --/| sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel
  --/|
  --/| There is no verified separate direct alias for Pact current slots, so use
  --/| the structured Pact path when you need that pool.
  --/|
  --/| NEVER TREAT THESE AS ONE POOL
  --/| A character can have normal and Pact slots at the same spell level.
  --/| Changing currentByLevel must not change currentPactByLevel, and changing
  --/| currentPactByLevel must not change currentByLevel.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial demonstrates that separation and restores every changed value.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --#title|[*S:character_name] - Beacon Spell Slots Tutorial

  --&CharacterID|[*S:character_id]

  --&NormalTotal|[*S:lvl1_slots_total:::0]
  --&NormalStart|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel->FIRST:::0]
  --&PactStart|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel->FIRST:::No Pact pool]

  --+|[c][b]Level 1 Slot Overview[/b][/c]

  --+Normal Slot Capacity|[&NormalTotal]
  --+Normal Slots Remaining|[&NormalStart]
  --+Compatibility Read|[*S:lvl1_slots_expended]
  --+Pact Slots Remaining|[&PactStart]

  --?"[&NormalTotal]" -le "0"|NoNormalSlots

  --+|[c][b]Normal Pool: Compatibility Alias[/b][/c]

  --/| Choose a temporary legal value.
  --=NormalTest|[&NormalStart] - 1
  --?"[&NormalStart]" -le "0"|[
    --=NormalTest|1
  --]|

  --/| Despite its historical name, this writes the remaining NORMAL slot count.
  --!c:[&CharacterID]|lvl1_slots_expended:[$NormalTest.Raw]

  --+Value Written|[$NormalTest.Raw]
  --+Alias Read Back|[*S:lvl1_slots_expended]
  --+Structured Normal Read|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel->FIRST]
  --+Pact Pool After Normal Write|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel->FIRST:::No Pact pool]

  --+|[c][b]Restore the Normal Pool[/b][/c]

  --/| Restore through the exact structured normal-slot path.
  --!c:[&CharacterID]|sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel->FIRST:[&NormalStart]

  --+Restored Normal Slots|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel->FIRST]
  --+Pact Pool Still|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel->FIRST:::No Pact pool]

  --?"[&PactStart]" -eq "No Pact pool"|NoPactWrite
  --?"[&PactStart]" -le "0"|NoPactAvailable

  --+|[c][b]Pact Pool: Structured Path[/b][/c]

  --=PactTest|[&PactStart] - 1

  --/| Pact slots use their own structured pool. Do not route this through the
  --/| normal lvl1_slots_expended compatibility alias.
  --!c:[&CharacterID]|sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel->FIRST:[$PactTest.Raw]

  --+Pact Value Written|[$PactTest.Raw]
  --+Pact Read Back|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel->FIRST]
  --+Normal Pool After Pact Write|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel->FIRST]

  --+|[c][b]Restore the Pact Pool[/b][/c]

  --!c:[&CharacterID]|sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel->FIRST:[&PactStart]

  --+Restored Pact Slots|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel->FIRST]
  --+Normal Pool Still|[*S:sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel->FIRST]

  --^Finished|

  --:NoPactWrite|
  --+|[c][b]No Pact Pool on This Character[/b][/c]
  --+Pact Test|Skipped. The normal-slot test above still demonstrates the normal pool.
  --^Finished|

  --:NoPactAvailable|
  --+|[c][b]No Pact Slots Currently Available[/b][/c]
  --+Pact Test|Skipped rather than adding a Pact slot that the character may not currently be entitled to use.
  --^Finished|

  --:NoNormalSlots|
  --+|[c][b]No Normal Level 1 Slots Found[/b][/c]
  --+Result|Select a Beacon spellcaster with normal level-1 slots and run the tutorial again.
  --X|

  --:Finished|
  --+|[c][b]What to Remember[/b][/c]

  --+Normal Current Pool|sheet->spellSlots->currentByLevel
  --+Pact Current Pool|sheet->spellSlots->currentPactByLevel
  --+Normal Compatibility Alias|lvlN_slots_expended means remaining normal slots in Beacon ScriptCards.
  --+Rule|Never combine, preserve, restore, or decrement the normal and Pact pools as if they were one value.

  --+|[c][b]Finished[/b][/c]

  --+Result|Normal and Pact slot state were handled as separate Beacon pools and all test changes were restored.
}}
